          <p class="mt-5 text-ops-subtle">One compose file. Backend and frontend in a single container, with Postgres alongside it. Production mode requires a real signing secret and real bootstrap credentials; weak defaults are refused at startup.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ops-muted">Prefer a binary? Linux and Windows builds are on the <a href={RELEASES_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-slate-300 underline decoration-ops-border underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-slate-400 focus-ring">releases page</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel rise lg:col-span-7" style="--i:1">
          <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-6 font-mono text-[13px] leading-7"><code><span class="text-ops-muted"># Clone it</span>
<span class="text-slate-200">git clone https://github.com/SpicyDaemon/OpsMender-AI</span>
<span class="text-slate-200">cd OpsMender-AI</span>

<span class="text-ops-muted"># Copy the example config, then set your model provider and API key</span>
